# Copy to .env (gitignored) for local runs; `npx expo start` reads it. EAS builds don't upload
# .env: they take the same names from each build profile's `env` in eas.json. Leave a value
# empty and Settings → About leaves that row out.
EXPO_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_URL=https://winzero.app/privacy
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_URL=https://winzero.app/support
# Win Zero Plus's store pages. Set, Win Zero offers Settings → About → Move to Win Zero Plus, and
# opens the page when Plus isn't installed. The iOS one stands in for the App Store page until
# Plus has an App Store id (https://apps.apple.com/app/id…), for QA only: a release build refuses
# it (npm run check:release:ios, build:android:upload). See docs/RELEASE.md for when to set them.
EXPO_PUBLIC_PLUS_STORE_URL_ANDROID=https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.e7systems.winzeroplus
EXPO_PUBLIC_PLUS_STORE_URL_IOS=https://winzero.app/
# Never set EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_VARIANT here: it picks Win Zero or Win Zero Plus (app.config.ts), and
# a value in .env would quietly turn every run and local build into Plus. Use the :plus scripts.
